  subgraph LAWS["⭐ THE LAWS (apply to every card, old + new)"]
    L1["/wow STANDARD (memory #15 · WOW_STANDARD.md): 'A Michelin chef explaining it to a grandma.' Every card = unique feel-line · didYouKnow moat (never reuse an angle) · buy-name ingredients (pp + total) · why-led method naming every make-or-break step · tip · storage+freezes+fridgeDays · goesWith verified vs real library (C4) · versions where warranted."]
    L2["LEAVENER LAW: yeast/baking powder/bicarb ALWAYS measured in g/ml, never 'to taste'. (§1 rolls: yeast 0.6g · sourdough starter 20g — all measured ✓)"]
    L3["SHELF-WOW LAW: remove & replace boring/googleable recipes, never disguise."]
    L4["VOICE STANDARD (global): match Fable's tone — fully detailed, why-led, sensory cues + temps + the reason behind each step. Milk 37–43°C (hotter kills yeast) · dough tacky not over-floured · fillings a wet-sand paste, softened not melted · roll tight · floss-slice · second rise shoulder-to-shoulder."]
    L5["C-RULES: C1 SA warmth where dish IS SA · C2 authentic name + gloss (SA names stand alone) · C3 honest swaps stated IN METHOD · C4 goesWith checked vs full name-set before writing."]
    L6["BOBOTIE RULE: master doughs = own cards · same-dough-same-dish-only-filling-swap = versions · genuinely distinct rolls = own cards + own moat. Never bundle distinct dishes to dodge photos (AI photos always achievable, never a reason to compromise — defer photo, never merge)."]
    L7["NON-NEG: real named spices · cured/salty/brined = no added salt + why stated (pepper always) · no retailer names · beginner-proof · names/photoName never changed on kept cards."]
    L8["SAMENESS: every page looks/functions the same; rooms differ only by photo+emoji. Uniformity ONLY via shared core.js + var(--token), never hand-rolled hex."]
  end
